      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yes. First party support for hip-based locomotion would be very useful.\nI have tried solutions like using DecaHub for hip based locomotion (which also happens to work with vive trackers), but they are a bit lacking as they work as a hack that changes the input direction of the stick.\nThus if you are running forwards and look to the side, you will start strafing, and in many worlds the strafe speed is less then the forwards movement speed so you end up moving slower, and also your movement animation/look in game is not as intended (e.g. running forward while looking to the side)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
