      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I know this is an old suggestion, but I would love the addition of hip-based locomotion in addition to the standard of head-based / controller-based. This would be a lot more natural for FBT users when walking and looking around at the same time, especially for OSC treadmill users.\n\nIf I remember right, DecaMove did something like this before they went under and I can't find a replacement online. This idea came back to me when trying to figure out how to get more fit in real life while still enjoying the beauty of VR (i.e. treadmill walking through large worlds).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-04T14:08:56.417Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As in: I'd like to be able to move in the horizontal direction that my hip points toward, not wherever i'm looking, so i can look around while still going forward, without having to adjust my thumbstick constantly.\nAlso so i don't start moving backwards when i look down or up and accidentally move past the 90 degree mark, which is ridiculous.\nOf course it would require a mechanism to prevent the behavior described above if the hip is pointing up/down/slightly further too.\nWhile you're at it, you can also add moving in the direction that you point with your left/right controller, which i personally dislike, but some people use it in games where they can.",
